# Guitar (issues 107, redrawn): 1x1 tile at the south wall (col 1, row 6 of the main room). The body sits north-east with its dark sound hole and the neck runs south-west to the headstock and mist tuners, lit from the top-left. It stands on a small folding stand (see `guitar-stand`) hidden under the body: while the guitar is played the piece shows `guitar-stand`, the empty stand, in that same place under where the body was.
size: 16x16
